    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Primary care physicians (PCPs) are a vital component of all healthcare systems, especially in rural areas. Routine visits with a PCP help establish relationships of trust between patients and physicians. Despite the benefits associated with regular PCP visits, there is a PCP shortage in rural communities across the globe, including rural communities in China. This thesis includes a cost-effectiveness analysis for increasing the number of PCPs who live and practice in rural China, measured specifically by the outcome of improved hypertension (HTN) care. Using the cost-effectiveness analysis to inform financial feasibility, the thesis concludes with three policy recommendations to help promote accessible healthcare in rural China.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
